From 5c235886f516f9488892c45edcf6c804a8a38f14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:15:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(multiaxis): rotary refusal names the 4-axis case

A model that is not a shape of revolution refuses the rotary kinds.
The refusal pointed only at the 5-Axis kinds, which a 4-axis machine
does not have. It now says that 4-axis work on a part clamped on A that
is not turned is not supported yet, and names the issue. The words
"share no rotation axis" and the 5-axis pointer stay.

Pinned by the_freeform_refusal_names_the_4_axis_case.

Refs #2772

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs      |  3 +-
 crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis.rs           |  2 +-
 .../src/multiaxis/axis_consensus_tests.rs     | 13 +++++++
 docs/decisions/2772-rotary-4axis-refusal.md   | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
